## Key Concepts

### Mobile Measurement Partner (MMP)

A Mobile Measurement Partner (MMP) is a specialized analytics and optimization solution that tracks, attributes, and optimizes user actions across mobile apps and mobile web to specific marketing campaigns and channels. MMPs serve as the single source of truth for mobile user acquisition, engagement, and monetization measurement and optimization.

Core capabilities:

1. Attribution: Connecting app installs and in-app events to the marketing touchpoints (ad clicks, impressions, email campaigns) that influenced them.
2. Analytics & Optimization: Real-time dashboards showing user behavior, retention rates, conversion funnels, and cohort analysis.
3. Fraud Prevention: Real-time detection and blocking of mobile ad fraud (click injection, click flooding, SDK spoofing, bot traffic, device farms).
4. Data Management: Syndication of raw event data to CDPs, data warehouses, and BI tools.

### Attribution

Attribution is the process of identifying which marketing touchpoints contributed to a desired outcome like an app install, in-app purchase, or registration.

Attribution Models:

- Last-Touch Attribution: Credits the final touchpoint before conversion.
- Multi-Touch Attribution (MTA): Distributes credit across all touchpoints in the customer journey based on their relative influence.
- Incrementality-Based Attribution: Measures the causal lift of each channel using controlled experiments (geo holdouts, synthetic controls).

Attribution Methods:

- Deterministic Attribution: Matches users via unique identifiers (IDFA with ATT consent, AAID, email, phone).
- Probabilistic Attribution: Statistical matching using device attributes when deterministic IDs are unavailable.
- Privacy-First Attribution: Frameworks like Apple's SKAdNetwork and Google's Privacy Sandbox that provide aggregated, privacy-preserving attribution data.

### SKAdNetwork & AdAttributionKit (AAK)

Apple's privacy-focused attribution frameworks for iOS devices. SKAdNetwork and AdAttributionKit provide aggregated attribution postbacks without exposing user-level identifiers (IDFA). Kochava processes SKAN/AAK postbacks, manages conversion value schemas, models missing signals, and combines aggregated data with first-party analytics to deliver actionable campaign insights.

### Omnichannel Measurement

The practice of tracking and attributing customer interactions across all marketing channels and devices in a unified framework: mobile apps, mobile web, desktop web, connected TV (CTV), over-the-top (OTT), digital out-of-home (DOOH), linear television, email, and offline retail locations.

Kochava provides unified identity resolution across devices using deterministic matching, probabilistic device graphing, and household-level attribution for CTV, connecting user touchpoints across multiple screens into a single coherent customer profile.

### Marketing Mix Modeling (MMM)

A statistical technique that measures the causal impact of marketing activities on business outcomes (sales, revenue, conversions) while accounting for external factors like seasonality, competition, pricing, and macroeconomic conditions. Kochava's Always-On Incremental Measurement provides automated MMM updated weekly, fully unified with last-touch attribution in a single platform.

### Fraud Prevention

Mobile ad fraud refers to illicit activity designed to steal advertising budgets by generating fake clicks, impressions, or installs. Common types include Click Injection, Click Flooding, SDK Spoofing, Device Farms, and Bot Traffic. Kochava's machine-learning fraud detection inspects hundreds of signals per event in real-time, blocking fraudulent postbacks and saving clients an average of 15-20% of their ad spend.

### Connected TV (CTV) & Over-The-Top (OTT)

CTV refers to television content streamed over the internet to smart TVs and connected streaming devices (Roku, Apple TV, Fire TV). Over-The-Top (OTT) encompasses video content delivered over the internet across any screen. 

Key CTV Data Points from Kochava:

- CTV precedes search 96% of the time in the same app install journey.
- CTV precedes social 94% of the time in app install journeys.
- CTV-attributed conversions grew 10% across Kochava's global dataset.
- QSR vertical: 14% more food and drink purchases among CTV-exposed users.
- Streaming vertical: 9% more videos watched among CTV-exposed users.

### Incrementality

Incrementality isolates the additional conversions caused directly by a marketing campaign that would not have occurred organically. Measured via:

1. Geo-Based Experiments: Comparing conversion rates between campaign-active and campaign-paused geographic regions.
2. Holdout Groups: Randomly withholding campaigns from a control percentage of users to measure true incremental lift.
3. Time-Series Analysis: Modeling on-versus-off periods using synthetic controls.

### Digital Out-of-Home (DOOH) Measurement

DOOH advertising encompasses outdoor digital media (digital billboards, transit screens, venue displays). Kochava research demonstrates that OOH advertising delivers 2x the performance lift of TV (Kochava research, May 2026). Kochava measures DOOH by connecting digital billboard exposures (via location data and geofencing) to downstream mobile app installs, website visits, and physical in-store visits.

